# Quality Gates / 品質ゲート

## Mandatory Checks / 必須チェック

No feature, fix, or documentation-driven code change is **complete** until all of the following pass:

```bash
npm run typecheck   # TypeScript strict — no casual `any`
npm run lint        # ESLint across workspaces
npm run test        # Unit and integration tests
npm run build       # Production build succeeds
```

Or run the aggregate:

```bash
npm run check
```

## What Each Gate Enforces / 各ゲートの役割

| Gate | Enforces |
|---|---|
| `typecheck` | Strict types; Application Service contracts; no silent `any` erosion |
| `lint` | Code style, import boundaries, a11y lint rules where configured |
| `test` | Domain logic, service orchestration, critical UI behavior |
| `build` | Next.js compilation, tree-shaking, no client secret leakage |

## Architecture Compliance / アーキテクチャ遵守

During review, also verify (not always automated):

- UI does **not** import Repository or Provider directly — Application Service layer only.
- No secrets in client-accessible code or public env vars.
- UI follows design system: no blue-purple gradients, glow/glass/AI decorations, giant KPI cards, card-grid layouts, or double scroll.
- IA follows **work units**, not feature/module names; internal names hidden from general users.
- Mobile layouts are purpose-built, not desktop columns stacked vertically.

## Product Integrity / プロダクト整合性

Every shipped screen should reinforce: Regapro AI is a **business OS**, not an AI chat app.

## CI Expectation / CI 期待値

These gates will run in CI. Local pass before push is required; fixing CI failures takes priority over new work.
